     "result_text_tail": "an, in exchange for not losing those SMB customers. Net revenue retention stays around 112\u2013113%. New customers still need to add about $1.5\u20132.6M of ARR to reach +15%. The pack has no data on new-customer bookings, so this needs checking with Finance.\n\n**Choices I made without you**\n- **Estimates:** the net figures rest on my assumptions, which are labelled \"est.\" on the slides and listed in Appendix A1. I scaled the 2023 SMB price response up to 12%, used the 2024 test gap for mid-market, and assumed enterprise customers don't churn over the rise.\n- **10% rather than 12% for mid-market:** 10% is the level that was actually tested.\n- **A test for SMB instead of a straight yes or no:** customers' current price sensitivity is the pack's biggest open question.\n- **Board churn figure:** the dashboard's \"1.4% \u2192 2.3%\" doesn't match the segment data under either weighting, so I flagged it in Appendix A2 rather than using it.\n\n**How I checked the layout:** PowerPoint, Keynote and Chrome couldn't run here, so I couldn't open the file in a real viewer. Instead, I rendered each slide with my own preview tool, checked every slide visually and fixed overlaps and overflowing text. The PDF comes from that same preview, so give the PowerPoint file a quick look in PowerPoint before circulating it. The charts are drawn as shapes, so they can be edited but aren't linked to data.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- Palisade_2027_Pricing_Recommendation.pptx\n- Palisade_2027_Pricing_Recommendation.pdf"
    }
